{:edb/db-before-t 1697 :edb/db-after-t 1698 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535010 50 #inst "2026-10-08T14:19:06.007Z" 13194139535010 true] [17592186105655 1020 #edb/ref 17592186326486 13194139535010 true] [17592186269129 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139535010 true] [17592186269129 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $A$, $B$, $C$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a=⟨2,1,-1⟩,\\,b=⟨3,-2,2⟩,\\,c=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠BAC=\\theta .$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964292/assets/285b8343208079181ac6036cf9ca16abc974d59b9262878ed40c0da9af5683d0.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,2⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩-⟨2,1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,-3,2⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{AC}}{|\\overset{\\to }{AB}||\\overset{\\to }{AC}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (-3)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}}\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{19}\\cdot \\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{418}})≈{54}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139535010 false] [17592186326486 1017 #edb/ref 17592186326487 13194139535010 true] [17592186326486 1089 "q-101506" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326486 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535010 true] [17592186326486 1100 "Find $∠QPR$ given the points $P(1,5,-1)$, $Q(5,1,1)$, and $R(2,5,0).$" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326486 1113 #uuid "823545bb-0540-59df-9354-6b5f7bce2ef1" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326486 1145 "Note that the position vectors of the points $P$, $Q$, $R$ are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=⟨1,5,-1⟩,\\,q=⟨5,1,1⟩,\\,r=⟨2,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $△PQR$ is shown (schematically) in the diagram below, where we denote $∠QPR=\\theta .$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046481/assets/3003f0cb329a8f8ef9bc315c70df4773ac1f0c54843dea1208c68bd0f6227bd1.png)\n\nFirst, we find the components of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨5,1,1⟩-⟨1,5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =⟨2,5,0⟩-⟨1,5,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the cosine of the angle between $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot \\overset{\\to }{PR}}{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}||\\overset{\\to }{PR}|} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{36}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}})={45}^{∘}.\n$$" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326488 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326489 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326490 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326491 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326492 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1041 "selection" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326491 13194139535010 true] [17592186326487 1110 #uuid "a136a672-4f55-5841-8df6-a4fe0d07dfcd" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326488 1034 "{60}^{∘}" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326488 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535010 true] [17592186326488 1111 #uuid "f1d923a3-db7f-532b-a813-4f0f8279c875" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326489 1034 "{90}^{∘}" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326489 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535010 true] [17592186326489 1111 #uuid "5918cfd2-1259-5fc3-8344-c3492582a735" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326490 1034 "{0}^{∘}" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326490 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535010 true] [17592186326490 1111 #uuid "f9f6c20b-558c-5896-a131-57fa545f27c1" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326491 1034 "{45}^{∘}" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326491 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535010 true] [17592186326491 1111 #uuid "75954da1-6d61-56d1-90af-589130ec7483" 13194139535010 true] [17592186326492 1034 "{30}^{∘}" 13194139535010 t